      "postID": "650afbb6cca589096b6577e8",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd go with a broader \"Photosensitive\" warning than explicitly \"Epileptic\", just because it's one of those things where some people will read the latter and not think it applies to them and then, whoops, migraine. \n\nDefinitely apply this to Avatar tags as well, so you can just disable anything with that tag from a setting.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-09-20T14:03:34.698Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since tags are now about to finally be used. Its as the title says. A tag for epileptic content so that people with epilepsi can hide that content. Of course it won't make it 100% safe as there will always be those people who won't use the tags. But just an idea I wanted to throw out there.",
